# Drafted by Gemini (R14 villagers), edited.

~ toma
Narrator: Silver dust sits gray in the creases of his knuckles. He holds a chunk of raw stone to his ear like a seashell.
dg_toma_flint [weary]: Hush now, little vein, I hear you. Keep your boots quiet, strangers, the rock's jumpy tonight. We dig the silver for their bell metal, and my brother walked up that hill and never walked back.
* How is the mine holding up? -> toma_mine
* What happens up at the monastery? -> toma_hill
* [if flag.axel_debts_asked and not flag.toma_paid and item:toma_hat] Give him his hat back -> toma_hat
* Leave him to his stone. -> END

~ toma_mine
dg_toma_flint [afraid]: The lode's running thin as a winter soup. Worse than that, the ore sounds frightened when you strike it, humming like a trapped bee.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Silver that rings when you strike it. I'd love a sample for the vials.
dg_toma_flint [weary]: Stone shouldn't shiver like flesh does, friend. It knows where we're sending it.
-> toma

~ toma_hill
dg_toma_flint [neutral]: You see those red windows shining on the snow? Nobody who goes in that gate with a question ever comes out with the answer.
dg_toma_flint [weary]: They come out smiling, or they come out as smoke.
-> toma

~ toma_hat
approve rook_coldwake +2 tobin_hayward +2: You returned Toma's hat and settled Axel's debt
take toma_hat
set toma_paid
gold +10
dg_toma_flint [smile]: Hmph. Still got my tallow stain on the brim. Take these coins for your trouble.
dg_toma_flint [sad]: I knew Axel before they put him in chains, you know. Good lad with a pickaxe, back when a man could still pay his own debts.
if flag.toma_paid and flag.dagny_paid and flag.halka_paid
quest axels_debts done
endif
-> toma

~ halka
Narrator: She stands by the cold hearth with her shawl pulled tight, watching the mountain road through a cracked pane.
dg_halka_wren [sad]: Mind your voices on the street, travelers. My boy rode out with the Sanguine Hunt last winter, and when he came back, his eyes belonged to someone else.
* Tell us about the Sanguine Hunt. -> halka_hunt
* Have you seen a Brightsinger pilgrim pass through? -> halka_pilgrim
* [if flag.axel_debts_asked and not flag.halka_paid and item:halka_letter] Give her the letter -> halka_letter
* We'll leave you in peace. -> END

~ halka_hunt
dg_halka_wren [afraid]: They ride down to the square at the Twilight bell, always the night after a Night of Flames, looking to drag in the impure.
dg_halka_wren [neutral]: If you mean to stop them, every shuttered house in this village is on your side.
set hunt_known
quest sanguine_hunt known
-> halka

~ halka_pilgrim
dg_halka_wren [neutral]: A tall dark lad with a short beard? Aye, I saw him go up the hill road two nights ago, singing a songbird hymn under his breath.
dg_halka_wren [weary]: The young stable hand from the monastery was whispering to him by the well before he climbed.
set stable_hand_clue
-> halka

~ halka_letter
approve tobin_hayward +3 rook_coldwake +2: You brought Halka her lost son's letter
take halka_letter
set halka_paid
Narrator: A small, dry cry catches in her throat as her thumb traces the crooked ink.
dg_halka_wren [sad]: That's his hand, alright, before the red glass took his mind. Thank you for bringing me the boy he used to be.
if flag.toma_paid and flag.dagny_paid and flag.halka_paid
quest axels_debts done
endif
-> halka

~ wren
Narrator: A small girl sits on afrosty crate, ticking off her fingers one by one whenever the wind brings a chime from the peak.
dg_wren_child [neutral]: Four for the matins, six for the smoke. My granddad helped cast the big bell up there, before the bats moved in.
* Which bell is that? -> wren_bell
* Stay warm, little one. -> END

~ wren_bell
dg_wren_child [neutral]: The big silver one in the high tower. Granddad says it had another name once, a proper miners' name stamped right on the lip.
dg_wren_child [sly]: Now they tell us it says Olaf's name instead, as if a friar ever swung a hammer.
set bell_rumour
-> wren

~ notice
Narrator: A parchment notice is nailed to the post with an iron spike, smelling faintly of tallow and old blood. It lists the signs of an impure heart alongside the promise of a heavy silver purse for any neighbor who names one.
-> END

~ hunt_ambush
quest sanguine_hunt known
Narrator: The Twilight bell fades into the snow as three armored riders tighten their girths in the square, a leashed bat-hound whining at their heels while pale faces watch from behind latched doors.
* Ambush them. -> ambush
* [ends:sanguine_hunt] Let them ride out. -> ride
* [if flag.maric_loosened] Watch the knight with the loose saddle. -> watch

~ ambush
approve lucan_houndstooth +3 rook_coldwake +3 tobin_hayward +2: You ambushed the Sanguine Hunt to protect the village
combat dg_hunt

~ watch
Narrator: As the third knight vaults into his stirrup, the loosened leather gives way and dumps him flat into the icy mud.
ser_maric_dunmore [afraid]: Back, beast! The girth was sabotaged, I tell you, watch its hooves!
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: A hunter who never inspects his own tack deserves a mouthful of slush.
landers_knight [angry]: Shut your mouth and draw steel, Maric, we have company!
-> ambush

~ ride
approve rook_coldwake -4 tobin_hayward -4 lucan_houndstooth -3: You let the Sanguine Hunt drag a villager away
quest sanguine_hunt rode_out
set hunt_gone
Narrator: Iron hooves thunder up the lane, a cottage door splinters in the dark, and the riders drag a weeping miner out by his collar. When the hoofbeats fade toward the mountain, the village is quieter than a grave.
-> END
